Q: Display the fraction for a group of functions I have a list of base(3) functions, e.g. a circle, and they are all unique. I am trying to display a fraction to show how many different values of height and radius there are. Here's an example of a set of three functions:
h = 3;
r = 7;
f1 = 3*sqrt(3);
f2 = 3;
f3 = 4;
